# Security review

For changes touching authentication, crypto, remote API, input parsing, or
network-exposed surfaces:

- Validate and bound all untrusted input at trust boundaries.
- Do not log secrets, tokens, or credentials.
- Prefer existing crypto APIs; do not roll custom primitives.
- Remote/navigation: allowlist redirects; use `crypto.getRandomValues` for tokens where applicable.
- Add or adjust regression tests when feasible.
- Update `docs/40_quality/security/**` or `.github/SECURITY.md` when durable
  threat model or procedure changes.
- Never open public issues for undisclosed vulnerabilities — see `.github/SECURITY.md`.
